Open folders from the desktop in the system's file manager.

The desktop stays PCManFM's, but a folder opened on it -- a double click, a
single click when that is set, the item menu's Open, Open in New Tab and
Open in New Window, the Trash and Documents icons -- now goes to the
application the system has set as the default for inode/directory, as every
other program's "open folder" does.  On LikeOS that is File Explorer
(likeos-explorer), so a folder window looks and behaves the same wherever it
was opened from.

PCManFM's own window remains the answer when the default is PCManFM itself,
when no default is set, or when the default cannot be started.  Running
pcmanfm directly still opens PCManFM windows.

